; name: Scorpion medallion
; group: Signs & inlays
; description: A scorpion medallion carved in relief from a picture (light stands high, dark goes deep; blurred 0.2 mm first to take out its grain) with a 60° V-bit in 45° raster lines 0.1 mm apart, cleared first with a Ø3 end mill so the V-bit only finishes, then cut out with an outside profile through the blank, held by tabs. Set the disc’s diameter, the margin round it, the blank’s thickness, the relief depth and the tabs with the variables; load your own picture into the engraving to carve something else.
; 
